{title: 562 - Come, Sing a Song of Harvest}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #562 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 562}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Come, sing a song of harvest, [Bb]Of [Bb7/Ab]thanks [Eb/G]for [Bb]daily [Eb]food!
[Bb]To [Fm/Ab]offer God [Cm/Eb]the [Db]first-fruits [C7/Bb]is [Fm/Ab]old as [Bb7]gratitude.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Long, long ago, the reapers, [Bb]before [Eb/G]they [Bb]kept [Eb]the feast,
[Bb]Put [Fm/Ab]first-fruits in [Cm/Eb]a [Db]basket, [C7/Bb]and [Fm/Ab]took it [Bb7]to the priest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]Shall we, sometimes [Ab/C]forgetful [Eb/G]oh [Bb]where [Eb]creation [Bb]starts,
[Bb]With [Fm/Ab]science [Cm]in [Fm]our [Db]pockets [Cm]lose [C7/Bb]wonder [Bb7]from our hearts?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Eb]May God, the great Creator, [Bb]to [Bb7/Ab]whom [Eb/G]all [Bb]life [Eb]belongs,
[Bb]Accept [Cm]these [Fm]gifts [Cm/Eb]we [Db]offer, [C7/Bb]our [Fm/Ab]service [Bb7]and our songs.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Eb]And lest the world go hungry [Ab/C]while [Bb7/Ab]we [Eb/G]ourselves are [Bb]fed,
[Bb]Make [Fm/Ab]each [Cm]of [Fm]us [Cm/Eb]more [Db]ready [C7/Bb]to [Fm/Ab]share our [Bb7]daily bread.
{end_of_verse}
